{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Reopened (operator-approved 2026-08-30): the documented reopen condition (\"reopen if the 2-port/long-drain ceiling ever becomes a problem in practice\") is now proven met by incident 2f46 (`beton-naval-eyas`). In-window: deploy_errors ×11 + mcp-retire-cap ×11 from a landing burst (14 MCP + 142 bot redeploys) hitting port-exhaustion, because uvicorn `timeout_graceful_shutdown` is coupled to the 1200s certified-op grace (`_mcp_health.py:743`) so a retiring MCP container holds a rotation port ~20 min even at 0 in-flight, and there are only 2 ports.\n\nRemediation approved (fixes 1+3; capacity Option 2 deferred): (1) decouple graceful-shutdown from the certified-op grace so a container fast-drains at 0 in-flight; (3) distinguish \"bot mid-redeploy\" from \"bot wedged\" before the drain-gate fail-opens (mechanism 2: `bot_in_flight_reviews()` returned -1 on an unreachable /health during the bot's own redeploy). The fix is being driven under bug 2f46 (proven Phase-1; relates_to this ticket). This ticket tracks the design-limitation record."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788144304859095413,"uuid":"38ae9454-ca55-440e-92df-1186f1f73595"}